menu "ArgonOS crypto"

    config ARGON_ENABLE_CRYPTO
        bool "Ed25519 and SHA-256/SHA-512 in the kernel"
        default y
        help
            The maths a signature needs, in the kernel rather than in every
            image that checks one: RFC 8032 Ed25519, FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 and
            SHA-512, and Monocypher under them.

            It is here because an application cannot afford it.  Monocypher is
            46 KB of C, an image has 64 KB of code for everything it does, and
            the shop was spending 11 KB of its 39 KB on its own copy - to check
            three signatures, in a program that also parses a catalogue, keeps
            a registry and speaks HTTP.  One copy in flash is shared by every
            image that needs it.

            Turn it off on a board that cannot spare the room.  api->crypto is
            then NULL, and the shop says "this firmware has no signature
            checking" and refuses to install anything - which is the honest
            answer, not a crash.  Nothing else in the tree depends on it.

endmenu
